System.Drawing.Common
---------------------

This product includes software from .NET (https://github.com/dotnet/runtime, branch release/6.0, commit 76b9680):
System.Drawing.Common 6.0 (src/libraries/System.Drawing.Common/src and the two Common/src interop files it uses),
licensed under the MIT License:

    Licensed to the .NET Foundation under one or more agreements.
    The .NET Foundation licenses this file to you under the MIT license.

It lives in src/drawingForCore.System.Drawing.Common; each file keeps its original header. The copy is made by
tools/lift/lift_drawing.py, which lists every change, and the per-file source is recorded in
tools/lift/manifests/System.Drawing.Common.tsv. The GDI+ engine in SkiaGdiPlus/ (from
tools/lift/additions/System.Drawing.Common/) is drawingForCore's own, under the MIT License. The assembly carries
System.Drawing.Common's public key (token cc7b13ffcd2ddd51, keys/System.Drawing.Common.snk) so that references to it
resolve; it is public signed, not signed by Microsoft. It uses SkiaSharp (https://github.com/mono/SkiaSharp, MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2015-2016 Xamarin, Inc., Copyright (c) 2017-2018 Microsoft Corporation) and the Skia native
library it ships (BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc.).

